# STRIDE Threat Analysis

## Threat 1: Price Manipulation During Checkout

| Field | Details |
|---------|---------|
| STRIDE Category | Tampering |
| Description | Attacker modifies product prices in checkout requests. |
| Attack Scenario | User intercepts request and changes price from $500 to $5. |
| Impact | Financial loss, fraud, inventory loss. |
| Likelihood | High |
| Mitigation | Server-side price validation and Stripe Checkout Sessions. |

---

## Threat 2: Session Hijacking

| Field | Details |
|---------|---------|
| STRIDE Category | Spoofing |
| Description | Attacker steals user session token. |
| Attack Scenario | Session cookie stolen via phishing or malware. |
| Impact | Unauthorized purchases. |
| Likelihood | Medium |
| Mitigation | HttpOnly cookies, MFA, token rotation. |

---

## Threat 3: Payment Data Interception

| Field | Details |
|---------|---------|
| STRIDE Category | Information Disclosure |
| Description | Payment information exposed during transmission. |
| Attack Scenario | MITM attack on insecure connection. |
| Impact | Data breach, compliance violations. |
| Likelihood | Medium-Low |
| Mitigation | TLS 1.3, HSTS, Stripe Elements. |

